    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d53-a1">

                <pb facs="0062" n="42" sameAs="frus:frus1864p3/pg42"/>

                <head>Mr. Welles to Mr.
                        Seward</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Navy Department,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1864-02-20"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >February</hi> 20, 1864.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your letter of the 17th instant, enclosing an extract from a despatch of Mr.
                    Dayton of the 26th ultimo, relative to the efforts that are to be made,
                    according to rumor, by the secessionists next spring, and expressing regret that
                    of the great number of our ships of war enough could not have been spared to
                    look after the small rebel cruisers now in French ports, &amp;c.</p>
                <p>In connexion with the remarks of Mr. Dayton I may be permitted to state that it
                    is not the want of ships that prevents a more vigorous pursuit and a more strict
                    surveillance upon the movements of the rebel cruisers at this time, but of <pb
                        facs="0063" n="43" xml:id="pg43"/> seamen to man them. It is a cause of
                    regret that our seamen have (under the promise of large bounties and the refusal
                    to credit, in ordering the draft, to the respective localities those who have
                    entered the navy) enlisted in the army, and thus left us without men to man our
                    ships.</p>
                <p>Very respectfully, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>GIDEON WELLES, <hi rendition="#italic">Secretary of the
                        Navy.</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Secretary of State.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
